# public_eval_dbff022c authoring notes

## Canonical rule

Find the unique solid 2×N or N×2 multicolor correspondence table.  Orient the
table so its key colors are the colors used by objects outside the table.  For
each zero-valued four-connected region that does not touch the canvas edge,
inspect its cardinal boundary.  When that boundary is a single mapped key
color, fill the entire hole with the corresponding table value.  Leave the
legend, frames, unmapped holes, and exterior background unchanged.

`reference.rkt` is a general implementation and is byte-identical to
`workspace/parametric/canonical.rkt`.  It reproduces every supplied train and
gold-labelled test pair.

## Episode-fixed extension

`finish_rule=highlight_dominant_fill` performs the canonical fill, totals the
newly filled interior area by mapped output color, selects the unique maximum,
and recolors only those newly filled cells with color 9.  Generated lessons
make the raw frame-frequency winner different from the filled-area winner.  The
retained counterfactual uses raw frame frequency, demonstrating the required
Stage-A-to-Stage-B dependency.

The sampler supports 2–6 demonstrations and 1–4 queries, keeps inputs matched
between settings, retains four private novel queries, privately permutes the
complete bank before taking a prefix, and contains a substantive 30×30 case.

## Evidence boundary

The task-local audit executes finite named rivals, protected-Racket labels,
private-field mutation checks, single-query public projections, and a source-
bound wrong-intermediate witness.  It is bounded reviewer evidence only: owner
registration, native qualification, acceptance, and any training admission are
separate and remain pending.
